#!/bin/bash
# 727 (Fri 27 Nov 2026 13:30, order from Peter's CEO chat: "Build the safe path to real money, in dry run only. Your readiness
# report of 27 November is the brief." Six points, quoted in the brief below.) NO REAL ORDER IS PLACED. The switch stays OFF.
# Nothing deleted: every file changed is copied to /root/pe-archive/placers_locked_27nov/ first.
B=/root/pe-builder; mkdir -p /root/pe-real $B/runs /root/pe-archive/placers_locked_27nov
cat > $B/BRIEF_safe_path.md <<'EOF'
You are a Builder on Peter Edwards' trading server. One long unattended job, start to finish, asking Peter nothing. Read /root/pe-builder/BRIEF_league.md first (all hard rules apply) and then /root/pe-queue/reports/ready_for_real.md, which is your brief: its sections 1, 2, 4 and 5 say what exists and what to build.

PETER'S ORDER, 27 Nov 13:30, word for word:
"Build the safe path to real money, in dry run only. 1. One program, and only one, may ever place a real order. Remove the order-placing ability from the nine old programs, or lock them so they cannot run. 2. A real off switch: the one placer checks it before every order and refuses if it is off. Leave it OFF. 3. A hard stake cap in the placer's own code, and a daily loss limit that stops it for the day. 4. Fix the guard so a failed login is reported as a failure, not as "0 bets". 5. Dry run it for 2 days against T1's signals: every order it would have placed, written down, compared with the trial record. They must match. 6. Proof for each of the five, in plain English: what you tested and what happened. No real order is placed. The switch stays off until Peter says yes in this chat, and only for a rule that has passed the proof gate."

ABSOLUTE LIMITS - these outrank finishing the job:
A. You never send a request to any Betfair (or other exchange) endpoint that places, cancels, replaces or updates an order - not once, not as a test, not with a tiny stake, not to "see the error". Read-only account calls (login, list cleared or current orders, account details) are allowed and only through /root/pe-queue/runner/creds.py. Every test of the sending path uses a fake sender object inside the test; the tests must also prove the real sender was not reached (count its calls = 0).
B. Do not create, remove, rename, empty or edit /root/REAL_MONEY_OFF. It exists and stays exactly as it is. Do not create any ON file or enable any control row in production. Tests of "switch on" behaviour pass temporary paths and a temporary control row INSIDE the test only; the production entry point has its paths written in the code, with no environment variable, command-line flag or config value that can redirect or skip a check.
C. Nothing deleted. Before changing any file copy it to /root/pe-archive/placers_locked_27nov/ keeping its path, and write MANIFEST.md there (file, checksum before, what was changed). No credentials, keys or passwords in any file you write, any log, any report or the repo (the repo is public). Do not print them. If you find secrets written in old code (the readiness report says bot_core.py has an app key and a database password), do not copy them into anything: say where they are and that they should be changed.
D. Do not edit /root/pe-sports/grid (trial.py, onetest.py, bankbook.py, the paper trader) - import and read. Do not disturb the recorders or the sessions running now. Memory: keep under 2 GB.
E. No cron lines for anything that could place an order. The dry runner may run under /root/pe-mechanic/watch.list as a keepalive because it cannot send.

THE FIVE, as build instructions:
1. ONE PLACER. /root/pe-real/placer.py is the only file on the server allowed to contain the order-sending call. Lock the nine old programs listed in the readiness report (and any other you find by searching every .py and .sh on the server for the order-placing, cancelling and replacing calls of all three exchanges - list what you searched): after the archive copy, replace each call site so it raises an error saying LOCKED 727, add the same refusal at the top of each program's entry point so it exits before logging in, remove the execute bit, confirm their cron lines and any systemd units, timers, keepalives and watch.list lines are off, and add a check, run hourly from the mechanic, that fails loudly to reports/breaks.md if any file other than /root/pe-real/placer.py contains an order-sending call or if a locked file has changed. PROOF: run each locked program's entry point and show it refuses before any network call; show the search finds the call in one file only.
2. THE OFF SWITCH. Before EVERY order, in this sequence, the placer must find all of: /root/REAL_MONEY_OFF absent; a file /root/pe-real/REAL_MONEY_ON present, owned by root, containing the exact name of one rule; that rule marked gate_passed with Peter's yes recorded (table real.gate: rule, date, who, the chat words) ; a control row enabled; a good login made in the last 10 minutes. Anything missing, unreadable or erroring = refuse and log why. The default with nothing set up is refuse. Dry mode is a separate thing: in dry mode the placer builds the full order, runs every check, writes the row, and stops one line before the sender; dry mode is the only mode started by this job. Leave it OFF: REAL_MONEY_OFF present, no ON file, real.gate empty, control row disabled. PROOF: known-answer tests for each condition alone and in combination (at least: OFF present + everything else on = refused; ON file missing = refused; ON names a different rule = refused; gate row missing = refused; login failed = refused; unreadable switch = refused; all good in the test with the fake sender = exactly one send), and the production state printed.
3. STAKE CAP AND DAILY LOSS LIMIT, as constants in placer.py itself, not in a table or config: MAX_STAKE = 2.00 (the first step of Peter's ladder; raising it is a code change Peter approves) and ABSOLUTE_MAX = 50.00 which no code path can exceed whatever MAX_STAKE says; backs only, LIMIT at the best back price, lapse at the off, no lay, no chasing, one order per match by a unique key in the database, at most 60 orders a day. DAILY_LOSS_LIMIT = 20.00: before each order add today's settled real loss to the worst case of every open order plus this one; at or past the limit the placer stops for the rest of the UK day, writes a BREAK, and a restart does not reset it (kept in the database, keyed by date). Also carry the bank book's live limits as the readiness report section 2.5 lists. PROOF: tests - £2.01 refused, £50.01 refused even with MAX_STAKE edited in the test, a lay refused, a second order on the same match refused, order 61 refused, the loss limit trips at the right order and stays tripped after a restart and clears next day.
4. THE GUARD. Fix real_money_guard.py (archive copy first): a failed or refused login, a timeout, or any error is written as a BREAK "guard could not log in / could not read" to reports/breaks.md and its own log, never as "0 bets"; "0 bets" is written only after a successful login and a successful read, with the time of both; it also reports whether REAL_MONEY_OFF is present and whether an ON file exists. Find out and fix why its login fails if it does (the recorders log in fine through runner/creds.py - use that). PROOF: force a bad login in a test and show the BREAK line; run it once for real and show the line it wrote.
5. THE DRY RUN, 2 DAYS, AGAINST T1. Build t1_live.py as the readiness report section 4.1 says (the same selection code as onetest.select(), acting at the start minus 125 s on live quotes), feeding placer.py in dry mode; table real.intended_orders (time, market, match, selection, side, price, stake £2, every check's result, would_send yes/no and why not). Start it, keep it alive under the mechanic, write the start time to /root/pe-real/dry_started (epoch seconds) at the moment the first full cycle runs clean. An hourly comparer writes /root/pe-queue/reports/dry_run_t1.md and pushes it: every intended order beside its T1 trial twin in grid.trial_trades (same market, same selection, same side; price within one tick; time within the cycle) - matched, intended with no twin, twin with no intended order, each unmatched one with its cause. They must match: for any mismatch find the cause; if the fault is in the new code fix it and say so (the 2 days restart from the fix); if the fault is in how the trial records, do not edit the trial - write it up as a finding. Also build the daily reconciler from section 5 in dry form, and do the read-only commission check (section 4.9).

REPORTS (plain English, loss or gain first, no code names without a plain explanation, one screen each):
- /root/pe-queue/reports/safe_path_727.md - for each of the five: what was built, what was tested, what happened (counts of tests passed and failed, the actual lines), and "DONE", "RUNNING" or "BLOCKED - why and what would unblock it". Line 1 always: "No real order was placed. Switch OFF: REAL_MONEY_OFF present yes/no, ON file absent yes/no, order calls to the exchange made by this job: 0." Push when items 1-4 are proved and the dry run has started. If any item is blocked, push at once with BLOCKED on line 2 and stop that item only.
- Commit and push each time: cd /root/pe-queue && git add reports/safe_path_727.md reports/dry_run_t1.md 2>/dev/null; git commit -qm "safe path to real money, dry run only: progress" ; git pull -q --no-rebase --no-edit ; env -u GITHUB_TOKEN git push -q
Finish by re-running the whole test file and the one-file search, and paste their last lines into the report. Then end the session; the dry runner and comparer keep going on their own.
EOF
cat > $B/BRIEF_safe_path_final.md <<'EOF'
You are a Builder on Peter Edwards' trading server: the closing check of the safe path to real money (job 727), two days after the dry run started. Read /root/pe-builder/BRIEF_league.md, /root/pe-builder/BRIEF_safe_path.md (its ABSOLUTE LIMITS A to E bind you exactly), /root/pe-queue/reports/safe_path_727.md and dry_run_t1.md. Place nothing; do not touch /root/REAL_MONEY_OFF; create no ON file.
DO: (1) confirm the dry runner ran the whole 2 days (gaps listed to the minute); (2) the final comparison: every order the placer would have placed against T1's trial record over the same hours - counts matched and unmatched, every unmatched one with its cause; verdict on one line: MATCH or NOT MATCHED; (3) re-run every test and the one-file search for order-sending calls, and run each locked old program once to show it still refuses; (4) confirm from Betfair's own record (read-only) that no real order exists on the account since 27 Nov 13:30 UK; (5) rewrite /root/pe-queue/reports/safe_path_727.md as the final report: line 1 the no-real-order line; line 2 "ALL FIVE DONE" or "BLOCKED: item n - why"; then for each of the five two or three plain sentences: what was tested and what happened, with the numbers; then exactly what a yes from Peter would switch on, step by step, and that nothing is switched on. Commit and push: cd /root/pe-queue && git add reports/safe_path_727.md reports/dry_run_t1.md && git commit -qm "safe path to real money: final report after 2-day dry run" && git pull -q --no-rebase --no-edit && env -u GITHUB_TOKEN git push -q. Then end the session.
EOF
cat > $B/run_safe_path.sh <<'SH'
#!/bin/bash
CL=$(cat /root/pe-watchman/claude_path); ts=$(date -u +%F_%H%M)
cd /root/pe-real && timeout -k 60 36000 "$CL" -p "$(cat /root/pe-builder/BRIEF_safe_path.md)" --allowedTools "Bash,Read,Write,Edit,Glob,Grep" --max-turns 900 --output-format text > /root/pe-builder/runs/${ts}_safe_path.log 2>&1
echo "safe path build session ended $(date -u '+%F %H:%M') exit $?" >> /root/pe-builder/sessions.log
date +%s > /root/pe-real/build_session_ended
SH
cat > $B/run_safe_path_final.sh <<'SH'
#!/bin/bash
CL=$(cat /root/pe-watchman/claude_path); ts=$(date -u +%F_%H%M)
cd /root/pe-real && timeout -k 60 7200 "$CL" -p "$(cat /root/pe-builder/BRIEF_safe_path_final.md)" --allowedTools "Bash,Read,Write,Edit,Glob,Grep" --max-turns 200 --output-format text > /root/pe-builder/runs/${ts}_safe_path_final.log 2>&1
echo "safe path final session ended $(date -u '+%F %H:%M') exit $?" >> /root/pe-builder/sessions.log
SH
chmod +x $B/run_safe_path.sh $B/run_safe_path_final.sh
nohup setsid $B/run_safe_path.sh > /dev/null 2>&1 < /dev/null &
sleep 15
echo "727 started $(date -u +%H:%M) UTC 27 Nov: safe path to real money, dry run only. Build session running: $(pgrep -fc '^/bin/bash /root/pe-builder/run_safe_path.sh') | REAL_MONEY_OFF present: $([ -e /root/REAL_MONEY_OFF ] && echo yes || echo NO) | ON file present: $([ -e /root/pe-real/REAL_MONEY_ON ] && echo YES || echo no) | free memory $(free -g | awk '/Mem/{print $7}') GB." >> /root/pe-queue/reports/running_now.md
cd /root/pe-queue && git add reports/running_now.md && git commit -qm "running now: 727" -q && git pull -q --no-rebase --no-edit && env -u GITHUB_TOKEN git push -q
